# Line endings (added when a second person started contributing).
#
# Windows and Mac/Linux end lines differently (CRLF vs LF). Without this
# file, each person's own Git settings decide what gets committed, and a
# contributor whose settings differ can commit a file with every line
# ending changed - a one-word edit then shows up as "every line of the
# file changed", which makes reviews unreadable and merges painful.
#
# "text=auto": Git stores every text file with LF in the repository (all
# 56 files already were), and each person's checkout uses whatever their
# own system prefers. Nobody has to configure anything.
* text=auto

# Never touch these: they're binary, and "fixing" their line endings
# would corrupt them.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.db   binary
